NEW GOLD LAWS


---

GL10 — Unified Format Law

All information entering JARVIS must conform to the JARVIS Hierarchy Protocol (JHP).

This includes:

GitHub

Supabase

MCP

Connectors

Logs

Governance


No alternate formatting standards are permitted inside the canonical repository.


---

GL11 — Mirror First Law

If information can be mirrored instead of duplicated, it must be mirrored.

Canonical truth may exist only once.

All secondary representations must reference canonical sources.


---

GL12 — Canonical Addressability Law

Every persistent object must possess:

JNL Address

Location

Tags

Anchor References

IndexSummary Entry


Objects lacking addressability are considered non-governed entities.


---

GL13 — Single Decode Path Law

Every object must be discoverable through:

JNL Address
OR
Location
OR
Tag
OR
Anchor

without requiring repository-wide search.


---

GL14 — Local Index Law

Every folder capable of containing persistent information must provide a local IndexSummary layer.

Routing should always begin locally before escalating globally.


---

GL15 — Registry Authority Law

Definitions may exist only once.

Tags, anchors, codes, governance rules, and addresses must be defined through Library Authority registries and mirrored elsewhere.


---

GL16 — Stable Structure Law

Structural identifiers must remain stable.

Content may change.

Addresses should not.

Line mappings, patch mappings, and routing references should remain immutable whenever possible.


