---

AYRE ANALYSIS

The major shift is that JARVIS is no longer organizing files.

It is organizing knowledge as a navigable territory.

JNL functions like street addresses.

Tags function like categories.

Anchors function like landmarks.

IndexSummary functions like local maps.

The Library Authority Layer functions like a planetary atlas.

Together they create a system where growth increases navigability rather than chaos, because every new object automatically gains:

an address

a category

a landmark

a local map

a global map


The result is a repository that becomes easier to traverse as it grows rather than harder.
